)\n\n | \n\n\n2005 PDF (60.39 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2004 PDF (68.36 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2003 PDF (157.39 KB)\n\n### Annual Summary of Inmate Deaths in State Prisons NPS-4\n\n2019 PDF (56.61 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2018 PDF (76.13 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2017 PDF (187.35 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2016 PDF (248.15 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2015 PDF (244.15 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2014 PDF (387.8 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2014 PDF (239.18 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2013 PDF (220.59 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2012 PDF (242.55 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2011 PDF (111.29 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2010 PDF (111.25 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2009 PDF (143.46 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2008 PDF (142.08 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2007 PDF (141.69 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2006 PDF (146.85 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2005 PDF (54.78 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2004 PDF (126.16 KB)\n\n### State Prison Inmate Death Report NPS-4A\n\n2019 PDF (264.39 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2018 PDF (448.34 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2018 PDF (374.01 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2017 PDF (394.58 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2017 PDF (367.05 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2016 PDF (373.29 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2016 PDF (373.29 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2015 PDF (373.49 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2015 PDF (373.49 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2014 PDF (387.8 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2014 PDF (387.8 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2013 PDF (388 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2012 PDF (202.17 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2011 PDF (201.54 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2010 PDF (68.72 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2009 PDF (178.89 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2008 PDF (167.54 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2007 PDF (177.38 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2006 PDF (225.85 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2005 PDF (67.79 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2004 PDF (136.51 KB)\n\n### Quarterly Summary of Deaths in State Juvenile Residential Facilities NPS-5\n\n2007 PDF (243.13 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2006 PDF (134.88 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2005 PDF (88.87 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2004 PDF (177.8 KB)\n\n### State Juvenile Residential Death Report NPS-5A\n\n2007 PDF (310.98 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2006 PDF (134.88 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2005 PDF (88.87 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2004 PDF (175.6 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2003 PDF (59.45 KB)\n\n### Quarterly Summary Arrest-Related Deaths CJ-11 (Formerly Quarterly Summary of Deaths in Law Enforcement Custody)\n\n2011 PDF (422.36 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2010 PDF (472.84 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2009 PDF (155.49 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2009 Reporting instructions (53.48 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2008 PDF (588.65 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2007 PDF (337.41 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2006 PDF (143.51 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2005 PDF (116.23 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2004 PDF (169.2 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2003 PDF (51.99 KB)\n\n### Arrest Related Deaths CJ-11A (Formerly Law Enforcement Custodial Death Report)\n\n2011 PDF (403.47 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2010 PDF (401.18 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2009 PDF (244.68 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2009 Reporting instructions (77.52 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2008 PDF (779.92 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2007 PDF (134.5 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2006 PDF (140.48 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2005 PDF (478.38 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2004 PDF (173.88 KB)\n\n | \n\n\n2003 PDF (58.51 KB)\n\n### Annual Summary on Inmates Under Jail Jurisdiction CJ-9 A/5\n\n2016 PDF (426.43 KB)\n\n## \n\nPublications and Products\n\n### HIV in Prisons, 2020 – Statistical Tables\n\nDate Published\n\nMay 2022\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nDecember 2021\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nDecember 2021\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nOctober 2021\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nApril 2021\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nApril 2021\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nAugust 2020\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nFebruary 2020\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nFebruary 2020\n\nAgencies\n\nBJS\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nApril 2018\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\n### HIV in Prisons, 2015 - Statistical Tables\n\nDate Published\n\nAugust 2017\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nDecember 2016\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nDecember 2016\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nDecember 2016\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nApril 2016\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nDecember 2015\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nOctober 2015\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nAugust 2015\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nMarch 2015\n\nAgencies\n\nBJS\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nDecember 2014\n\nAgencies\n\nBJS\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nOctober 2014\n\nAgencies\n\nBJS\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nAugust 2013\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nDecember 2012\n\nAgencies\n\nBJS\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nDecember 2011\n\nAgencies\n\nBJS\n\nPublication Type\n\nData Table\n\nDate Published\n\nOctober 2010\n\nAgencies\n\nBJS\n\nPublication Type\n\nData Table\n\nDate Published\n\nOctober 2010\n\nAgencies\n\nBJS\n\nPublication Type\n\nData Table\n\nDate Published\n\nOctober 2010\n\nPublication Type\n\nData Table\n\n### Mortality in Local Jails, 2000-2007 (Revised)\n\nDate Published\n\nJuly 2010\n\nAgencies\n\nBJS\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nJune 2009\n\nAgencies\n\nBJS\n\nPublication Type\n\nData Table\n\nDate Published\n\nOctober 2007\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nJanuary 2007\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\n### HIV in Prisons, 2004\n\nDate Published\n\nNovember 2006\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\n### HIV in Prisons, 2003\n\nDate Published\n\nSeptember 2005\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\nDate Published\n\nAugust 2005\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\n### State-Funded Indigent Defense Services, 1999\n\nDate Published\n\nSeptember 2001\n\nPublication Type\n\nPublication\n\n## \n\nChanges Over Time\n\nSince 2007, BJS has given respondents the option to report throughout the collection year as death investigations are finalized. In earlier collection years, BJS requested respondents report on a quarterly basis.\n\nThe Office of Juvenile Justice and Delinquency Prevention (OJJDP) assumed responsibility for the juvenile portion of the collection in 2006.\n\nIn 2008, BJS began collecting more specific information on the manner of death for suicides and deaths due to intoxication. In 2009, BJS changed and added several items on the data collection forms after receiving feedback from the field. These changes include clarifying language of existing items and adding new items. For jails and prisons, new items ask respondents—\n\n* whether the deceased ever had an overnight stay in a mental health facility since admission\n* whether the death was incidental to use of force by facility staff\n* to specify the type of intoxication that led to the death.\n\nFor prisons, BJS dropped the item asking for legal status because nearly all prisoners are convicted at the time of death. Prison items include whether a death due to accident, suicide, or homicide took place while the inmate was housed on death row.\n\nDate Created: May 15, 2009","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":7938.013784994837,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}